From: cidwel <cidwel@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_pas: do not drop the proxy votes

On sm8150 the modem boots, but the QLink link to the transceiver fails to
wake up from hibernation: the modem's own log shows "Entered Qlink
Hibernation mode" and then the assertion rflm_qlnk_ls_retry_cnt < 2 fires
(Link Start failed twice). The RF scheduler also reports that every event
overruns its window by a constant 7.0 %, which suggests the modem is
running slower than its firmware assumes.

Mainline drops the proxy votes (CX, MSS and the XO clock) as soon as the
peripheral signals handover; downstream keeps them at TURBO. This
experiment keeps them, to see whether the link stops failing.

--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -387,13 +387,8 @@
 {
 	struct qcom_pas *pas = container_of(q6v5, struct qcom_pas, q6v5);
 
-	if (pas->px_supply)
-		regulator_disable(pas->px_supply);
-	if (pas->cx_supply)
-		regulator_disable(pas->cx_supply);
-	clk_disable_unprepare(pas->aggre2_clk);
-	clk_disable_unprepare(pas->xo);
-	qcom_pas_pds_disable(pas, pas->proxy_pds, pas->proxy_pd_count);
+	/* TEST sm8150: keep the proxy votes instead of dropping them. */
+	(void)pas;
 }
 
 static int qcom_pas_stop(struct rproc *rproc)
